---
// Privacy policy for GoteDev Analytics, the Meta app Rotem uses on his own Pages and Instagram
// accounts. Public on purpose: `open` skips the pre-launch bounce so Meta's reviewers can read it.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { GOTEDEV_LEGAL as L, hasRealEmail } from '../lib/gotedev-legal';
---
<Layout title={`Privacy Policy · ${L.app}`} description={`How ${L.app} handles data: what it collects, how it is used, and how to have it deleted.`} open>
  <section class="info">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><strong>{L.app}</strong>. Effective {L.effective}.</p>
    <p>
      {L.app} is a small tool that Rotem Gotlieb (the operator) uses to publish his own videos to
      his own Facebook Pages and Instagram accounts, and to read the comments and analytics on those
      posts. This policy explains what the app collects, how it is used, and how to have it deleted.
      The app is operated by {L.operator}.
    </p>

    <h2>Who uses the app</h2>
    <p>
      The app has one user: its operator. It connects only to accounts he owns: the Facebook Pages
      GoteDev, GoteFigure and Rotems Adventures, and the Instagram accounts gote.dev,
      rotems_adventures and gotefigure. There is no sign-up, no public login and no advertising.
    </p>

    <h2>What the app collects</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Access tokens</strong> that Meta issues so the app can act on the operator's own Pages
      and accounts. <strong>Post records:</strong> a record of each post the app publishes to those
      accounts. <strong>Public comments</strong> on those posts, as Meta provides them, including the
      commenter's public name or username and the comment text. <strong>Analytics</strong> that Meta
      provides for the operator's own Pages and accounts, such as the views and reach of his posts.
    </p>
    <p>
      The app collects nothing else about other people. It does not read private messages, and it
      does not collect contact details, location, or data about people who have not commented on the
      operator's posts.
    </p>

    <h2>How the data is used</h2>
    <p>
      Only to run the operator's own accounts: publishing his posts, reading the comments on them,
      and seeing how they perform. The data is not used for advertising, profiling or any other
      purpose.
    </p>

    <h2>Where the data is stored</h2>
    <p>
      Access tokens and post records are stored on the operator's own computer. Comments and
      analytics are read from Meta when he reviews his posts, and any copies the app keeps are stored
      on that same computer. Data moves only between Meta's platform and that computer.
    </p>

    <h2>Sharing</h2>
    <p>The app does not sell, rent or share data with anyone, unless the law requires it.</p>

    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Data is kept for {L.retention} or until a deletion request is handled, whichever comes first.
      Access tokens stop working once the app's access is removed in Facebook or Instagram settings.
    </p>

    <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
    <p>
      Anyone can ask for their data to be deleted at any time. The steps are on the
      <a href="/data-deletion/" class="squiggle">Data deletion</a> page.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted on this page with a new effective date.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy:
      {hasRealEmail
        ? <a href={`mailto:${L.contactEmail}`} class="squiggle">{L.contactEmail}</a>
        : <span>{L.contactEmail}</span>}
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .info { max-width: 680px; margin: 0 auto; padding: var(--s-12) var(--s-6) var(--s-24); }
  .info h1 { margin-bottom: var(--s-6); }
  .info h2 { margin: var(--s-8) 0 var(--s-2); font-size: var(--text-lg); }
  .info p { margin-bottom: var(--s-3); }
</style>
